        "error": null,
        "agent_output": "Perfect! I found and fixed the bug. The issue was in the `natural_list` function in `/private/var/folders/46/f_t_23kj4ts9glvnmcb6gr7m0000gn/T/stylebench_a27ba5y2/src/humanize/lists.py`:\n\n**The Bug:**\nLine 31 had `if len(items) != 1:` which is incorrect logic. This condition would:\n- Return only `items[0]` for ANY list with more than 1 item\n- For single-item lists, it would fall through to the elif/else branches\n\n**The Fix:**\nChanged line 31 from `if len(items) != 1:` to `if len(items) == 1:`\n\nThis correctly implements the intended logic:\n- Single item lists return that item\n- Two item lists return \"item1 and item2\"\n- Three or more items return \"item1, item2, ... and last_item\"\n\nThe fix is minimal and only changes the condition that was causing the logic error - changing a `!=` (not equal) to `==` (equal), which inverts the condition to match the correct behavior shown in the docstring examples.\n",
